167
00:08:54,267 --> 00:08:57,634
Reporting live, Robin Scherbatsky,
Metro News 1.

168
00:09:00,439 --> 00:09:03,602
Joel Adams wants to see you in his office.

169
00:09:05,378 --> 00:09:10,111
Before you say anything, I just wanna say
I really like working here at Metro News 1.

170
00:09:10,216 --> 00:09:13,481
That's great. So my dog keeps going...

171
00:09:17,557 --> 00:09:18,524
What?

172
00:09:18,624 --> 00:09:21,422
What? Well, you have dogs, right?
What do you think that means?

173
00:09:21,527 --> 00:09:22,789
Take him to the vet.

174
00:09:24,196 --> 00:09:26,721
Genius. That's one I owe you.

175
00:09:27,533 --> 00:09:29,228
- Was that all?
- Yeah.

176
00:09:32,538 --> 00:09:35,473
- And nothing about the twins story?
- Oh, yeah. Great job on that one.

177
00:09:35,575 --> 00:09:37,566
New York loves you.
You're a superstar. Bye-bye.

178
00:09:39,946 --> 00:09:41,106
<i>That's when Robin realized</i>

179
00:09:41,213 --> 00:09:44,614
<i>no one, not even her boss,</i>
<i>watched Metro News 1,</i>

180
00:09:55,995 --> 00:09:57,019
Hi.

181
00:09:59,465 --> 00:10:02,400
Natalie, come on.
I just wanna say I'm sorry.

182
00:10:02,602 --> 00:10:04,832
I only came down here
'cause you wouldn't take my call.

183
00:10:04,937 --> 00:10:07,963
Hey, here's an idea.
Why don't you leave a message?

184
00:10:10,443 --> 00:10:12,502
Good one. Okay, fine.

185
00:10:12,612 --> 00:10:14,773
I'm just gonna leave
this sock monkey here.

186
00:10:15,514 --> 00:10:16,845
Goodbye.

187
00:10:22,688 --> 00:10:25,418
Okay, okay. Look, look, look,
I know you're mad, but

188
00:10:26,125 --> 00:10:28,650
happy birthday, three years ago.

189
00:10:28,761 --> 00:10:31,252
Oh, yeah? Up yours, three years ago.

190
00:10:31,530 --> 00:10:34,363
Look, look, I was an idiot,
leaving that message.

191
00:10:34,467 --> 00:10:37,925
- I realize how much that sucked.
- No, you don't.

192
00:10:38,504 --> 00:10:41,029
<i>Maybe we should just call it a day,</i>

193
00:10:42,341 --> 00:10:44,275
<i>But you're awesome,</i>

194
00:10:45,911 --> 00:10:47,776
<i>Okay, bye,</i>

195
00:10:50,249 --> 00:10:51,341
Surprise.

196
00:10:53,452 --> 00:10:57,149
There was a surprise party that night?
How come nobody told me?

197
00:10:57,356 --> 00:11:00,291
People think I can't keep a secret,
but I totally can.

198
00:11:00,960 --> 00:11:02,325
Sorry. Not the issue.

199
00:11:02,595 --> 00:11:06,861
Look, Natalie, I was just a stupid kid
back then, terrified of commitment.

200
00:11:06,966 --> 00:11:10,197
And I suppose you're suddenly ready
to get married and settle down?

201
00:11:10,603 --> 00:11:14,004
Well, yeah, actually.
I'm a different guy now.

202
00:11:15,675 --> 00:11:17,108
Give me another chance.

203
00:11:17,276 --> 00:11:20,074
You must think I have
absolutely no self-respect.

204
00:11:20,179 --> 00:11:22,204
Come on. Just a cup of coffee.

205
00:11:24,784 --> 00:11:27,912
Please, Natalie, give the guy a chance.

206
00:11:28,688 --> 00:11:31,088
Self-respect is overrated.

207
00:11:37,063 --> 00:11:38,257
Wow!

208
00:11:39,432 --> 00:11:40,729
Maybe it was the caffeine,

209
00:11:40,833 --> 00:11:43,131
but you really brought your game up
to a whole new level.

210
00:11:43,235 --> 00:11:46,727
Thanks.
I did just start subscribing to <i>Esquire,</i>

211
00:11:47,039 --> 00:11:48,836
They have some helpful columns.

212
00:11:48,941 --> 00:11:52,775
The following is from the October issue.

213
00:11:54,080 --> 00:11:56,514
<i>So Natalie and I</i>
<i>started dating again,</i>

214
00:11:56,615 --> 00:11:58,810
<i>And, just like that, it all came back,</i>

215
00:11:58,918 --> 00:12:00,317
<i>The tea candles,</i>

216
00:12:00,553 --> 00:12:01,952
<i>The sock monkeys,</i>

217
00:12:02,054 --> 00:12:04,454
<i>Belle and Sebastian, All of it,</i>

218
00:12:04,657 --> 00:12:07,387
<i>It seemed like happily-ever-after</i>
<i>wasn't far off,</i>

219
00:12:08,127 --> 00:12:10,994
Well, I better run.
I have my Krav Maga class in half an hour.

220
00:12:11,097 --> 00:12:14,066
Krav Maga.
How cool is it that she does Krav Maga?

221
00:12:14,500 --> 00:12:16,195
Thanks, honey.

222
00:12:17,169 --> 00:12:18,227
- Bye, guys.
- Bye.

223
00:12:18,337 --> 00:12:19,304
- Bye.
- Take it easy.

224
00:12:20,673 --> 00:12:22,140
Dude, what's Krav Maga?

225
00:12:22,241 --> 00:12:24,732
I have no idea. Some kind of yoga?

226
00:12:25,678 --> 00:12:27,475
You know, that Natalie, she's good times.

227
00:12:27,580 --> 00:12:29,445
Yeah, she's, like, the best girl
you've dated in years.

228
00:12:29,548 --> 00:12:32,073
- Yeah, Ted, hold on to that one.
- Yeah.

229
00:12:32,218 --> 00:12:34,243
I have to break up with her.

230
00:12:38,891 --> 00:12:41,223
I don't get it, man. Natalie's awesome.

231
00:12:41,327 --> 00:12:44,490
I know. She's terrific,
but I have to break up with her.

232
00:12:45,831 --> 00:12:49,062
Why couldn't you leave
that poor girl alone?

233
00:12:49,168 --> 00:12:50,897
I know. I hate this.

234
00:12:51,003 --> 00:12:53,665
These past three weeks have been great.
I should be in love with her,

235
00:12:53,773 --> 00:12:55,900
but I'm not feeling that thing.

236
00:12:56,008 --> 00:12:57,805
It's ineffable.

237
00:12:57,910 --> 00:13:00,071
Ineffable. Good word.

238
00:13:00,946 --> 00:13:02,379
So when are you gonna do it?

239
00:13:02,481 --> 00:13:05,109
She's probably on the subway by now.
You could call her voicemail.

240
00:13:05,217 --> 00:13:07,981
Beep. Dumped. Click. Done.

241
00:13:08,788 --> 00:13:12,280
I have to do this face-to-face. I just...
I don't know what I'm gonna say.

242
00:13:12,391 --> 00:13:15,519
- "I'm not ready for a commitment."
- Oh, that's such a cliché.

243
00:13:15,628 --> 00:13:17,858
It's not a cliché. It's a classic.

244
00:13:18,063 --> 00:13:20,554
It's the <i>Stairway to Heaven</i>
of break-up lines.

245
00:13:20,833 --> 00:13:23,768
- Well, I think Natalie deserves better.
- Better.

246
00:13:23,903 --> 00:13:27,236
There's no "better" in breaking up.
There's only less awful.

247
00:13:27,339 --> 00:13:30,672
A cliché is a cliché for a reason.
It's comforting.

248
00:13:30,776 --> 00:13:33,939
It doesn't matter. I already told her
I am ready for a commitment so...

249
00:13:34,380 --> 00:13:37,144
Oh, my God, there's no way out.
I'm gonna have to marry her.

250
00:13:37,249 --> 00:13:39,877
No, no. We're gonna get you
out of this. Okay.

251
00:13:40,286 --> 00:13:43,187
How about, "It's not you. It's me"?

252
00:13:44,390 --> 00:13:45,550
Six words.

253
00:13:45,658 --> 00:13:48,149
"You look fat in those jeans."
You're free to go.

254
00:13:49,595 --> 00:13:52,621
Ted, have you considered
telling her the truth?

255
00:13:54,900 --> 00:13:56,458
Seriously, honey, men are working here.

256
00:13:57,903 --> 00:14:01,066
Ted, what is the truth?
Why do you wanna break up with her?

257
00:14:01,273 --> 00:14:03,571
The truth? She's not the one.

258
00:14:03,909 --> 00:14:07,276
- So tell her that.
- Oh, you can't tell her that. That's horrible.

259
00:14:07,379 --> 00:14:10,075
Why? What is so horrible about that?

260
00:14:10,282 --> 00:14:13,877
Yeah, what is so horrible about that?
She's not the one.

261
00:14:13,986 --> 00:14:16,045
Why is that such a heart-breaking thing
to hear?

262
00:14:16,155 --> 00:14:18,749
The chances of one person
being another person's "the one"

263
00:14:18,858 --> 00:14:20,416
are, like, six billion-to-one.

264
00:14:20,526 --> 00:14:22,960
Yeah, you have better chances
of winning the lottery.

265
00:14:23,062 --> 00:14:26,088
Exactly. You wouldn't take it personally
if you lost the lottery.

266
00:14:26,198 --> 00:14:29,599
All right, man, tell her the truth.
She's gonna cry.

267
00:14:29,702 --> 00:14:33,035
Yeah, and he's gonna sit there,
and he's gonna take it like a man.

268
00:14:33,138 --> 00:14:36,232
- I have to do the mature thing.
- Wanna talk mature?

269
00:14:36,342 --> 00:14:39,971
I just wrapped up a live newscast
by honking my own boobs.

270
00:14:41,080 --> 00:14:43,173
And great TV was had by all.

271
00:14:45,150 --> 00:14:46,845
All right, Scherbatsky, new challenge.

272
00:14:46,952 --> 00:14:50,046
And this one's big,
but so is the cash reward.

273
00:14:50,155 --> 00:14:53,249
For $1,000... You heard me.

274
00:14:53,359 --> 00:14:56,692
All you have to do is get up there
on the news and do one of these.

275
00:15:04,470 --> 00:15:06,870
- What the hell is that?
- The Ickey Shuffle.

276
00:15:06,972 --> 00:15:09,566
Then, as you do it, you say this,

277
00:15:09,675 --> 00:15:13,839
"Elbert 'Ickey' Woods,
the Bengals were fools to cut you in '91.

278
00:15:13,946 --> 00:15:16,176
"Your 1,525 rushing yards

279
00:15:16,282 --> 00:15:18,546
"and your 27 touchdowns
will not be forgotten.

280
00:15:18,651 --> 00:15:23,247
"So, Coach Dave Shula, screw you
and your crappy steakhouse."

281
00:15:24,757 --> 00:15:26,554
Just write it down for me.

282
00:15:27,326 --> 00:15:30,295
What do I care? It's not like
anyone's watching anyway, right?

283
00:15:32,364 --> 00:15:34,696
And she's gonna cry.

284
00:15:36,502 --> 00:15:38,800
Sloth love Chunk.

285
00:15:39,838 --> 00:15:41,271
Thanks, Lil.

286
00:15:42,141 --> 00:15:44,939
<i>So the next night,</i>
<i>I took Natalie out to dinner</i>

287
00:15:45,044 --> 00:15:46,602
<i>to do the mature thing,</i>

288
00:15:47,413 --> 00:15:49,506
Look, Natalie, there's something
I have to say.

289
00:15:49,615 --> 00:15:51,708
Oh, wait, wait.
There's something I have to say first.

290
00:15:51,817 --> 00:15:56,413
Today at work I had not one, not two,
but three birthday cakes.

291
00:15:56,522 --> 00:15:59,013
So, tonight, can we just skip the cake?

292
00:15:59,825 --> 00:16:01,725
- Today is your birthday?
- Yeah.

293
00:16:01,827 --> 00:16:03,727
No, it's okay.
I wasn't telling anyone about it.

294
00:16:03,829 --> 00:16:05,694
Today is your birthday!

295
00:16:09,201 --> 00:16:12,364
- I didn't get you anything.
- Oh, it's okay.

296
00:16:13,172 --> 00:16:15,936
You know, you've already given me
the best present of all.

297
00:16:17,309 --> 00:16:19,174
I can trust again.

298
00:16:22,114 --> 00:16:23,445
You're welcome.

299
00:16:28,921 --> 00:16:30,752
Oh, so much more wine.

300
00:16:37,963 --> 00:16:40,989
Henry, as New York's oldest
hansom-cab driver,

301
00:16:41,100 --> 00:16:42,260
you've seen quite a lot.

302
00:16:42,668 --> 00:16:46,536
<i>In your past 60 years on the job,</i>
<i>what is your most exciting memory?</i>

303
00:16:47,239 --> 00:16:48,706
<i>Well...</i>

304
00:16:48,807 --> 00:16:51,435
- This is it.
- Oh, boy, here we go.

305
00:16:51,543 --> 00:16:54,239
Everyone, everyone, if I may
direct your attention to the television.

306
00:16:54,346 --> 00:16:56,678
You are about to see something amazing.

307
00:16:56,782 --> 00:16:59,342
<i>And then in '72,</i>

308
00:16:59,885 --> 00:17:04,788
<i>Mickey Mantle rode in my cab</i>
<i>for the fourth time,</i>

309
00:17:04,990 --> 00:17:07,117
Come on, baby, bring it home.

310
00:17:07,226 --> 00:17:10,024
<i>But the most exciting moment,</i>

311
00:17:10,462 --> 00:17:13,829
<i>that would have to be this one, right now,</i>

312
00:17:14,733 --> 00:17:18,669
<i>- What?</i>
<i>- Look at me, I'm on TV,</i>

313
00:17:19,338 --> 00:17:22,364
<i>I never thought I'd have my story told,</i>

314
00:17:23,409 --> 00:17:25,843
<i>Thank you, Miss Robin Scherbatsky,</i>

315
00:17:26,545 --> 00:17:27,671
<i>Thank you,</i>

316
00:17:27,780 --> 00:17:31,910
<i>And, right then, Aunt Robin</i>
<i>realized how important her job truly was,</i>

317
00:17:32,017 --> 00:17:34,508
<i>It's an honor to tell your story, Henry,</i>

318
00:17:35,854 --> 00:17:39,517
<i>You know, Metro News 1</i>
<i>may not be number one in viewership,</i>

319
00:17:39,625 --> 00:17:41,752
<i>but this reporter takes pride in...</i>

320
00:17:43,162 --> 00:17:46,325
<i>ROBIN; Oh, my God,</i>
<i>I'm covered in horse crap!</i>

321
00:17:46,832 --> 00:17:48,857
<i>And it's in my hair!</i>

322
00:17:49,001 --> 00:17:51,333
- You planned that?
<i>- My knee!</i>

323
00:17:51,470 --> 00:17:55,236
No, Marshall.
That was beyond my wildest dreams.

324
00:17:57,409 --> 00:17:59,434
So if you ever come to Alabama,

325
00:17:59,545 --> 00:18:02,309
my mom throws
these huge crawfish boils,

326
00:18:02,414 --> 00:18:04,780
and she's just dying
to meet you, by the way.

327
00:18:04,883 --> 00:18:06,578
Look, Natalie,
there's something I have to say,

328
00:18:06,685 --> 00:18:08,516
and there's no good way to say it.

329
00:18:09,755 --> 00:18:11,245
I wanna break up.

330
00:18:12,291 --> 00:18:14,225
I don't think you're the one for me.

331
00:18:14,960 --> 00:18:18,020
I don't wanna waste your time,
because I really like you.

332
00:18:18,964 --> 00:18:21,626
I wanna do right by you,
and I think the best way for me to do that

333
00:18:21,733 --> 00:18:24,827
is just to be honest. I'm sorry.

334
00:18:28,373 --> 00:18:29,840
Just let it out.

335
00:18:31,076 --> 00:18:32,475
They're only tears.

336
00:18:37,649 --> 00:18:39,742
I'm not the one for you!

337
00:18:40,252 --> 00:18:42,652
I'm sorry. I just... I thought
the mature thing to do would be...

338
00:18:42,754 --> 00:18:45,154
- It's my birthday.
- Yes, I know. I didn't realize that it was...

339
00:18:45,257 --> 00:18:48,749
It's my birthday, and you're telling me
I'm not the one for you?

340
00:18:48,861 --> 00:18:51,694
It's really not such a big deal.
I mean, it's the odds.

341
00:18:51,797 --> 00:18:53,560
It's like you lost the lottery.

342
00:18:54,032 --> 00:18:55,863
Oh, so dating you is like
winning the lottery?

343
00:18:55,968 --> 00:18:59,460
- No, no, no. I didn't mean that.
- Okay, so what's the problem?

344
00:19:00,506 --> 00:19:02,667
- I can't explain it.
- Try.

345
00:19:02,774 --> 00:19:06,642
- It's ineffable.
- I'm not F-able?

346
00:19:07,279 --> 00:19:11,147
No, no, no, no, ineffable.
"Ineffable" means it can't be explained.

347
00:19:11,250 --> 00:19:13,616
- Oh, so I'm stupid?
- Oh, God, what's going on?

348
00:19:13,719 --> 00:19:16,916
Okay, what's going on is
you broke my heart

349
00:19:17,022 --> 00:19:20,116
over my answering machine,
on my birthday,

350
00:19:20,225 --> 00:19:22,853
waited three years for me to get over you,

351
00:19:22,961 --> 00:19:25,156
tracked me down,
begged me to go out with you again,

352
00:19:25,264 --> 00:19:28,461
only so you could dump me
three weeks later,

353
00:19:28,567 --> 00:19:30,660
again on my birthday!

354
00:19:30,769 --> 00:19:33,533
No, it's not like that. I'm just...

355
00:19:33,639 --> 00:19:35,573
- It's...
- What?

356
00:19:35,674 --> 00:19:38,165
I'm just, like, super busy right now.

357
00:19:39,411 --> 00:19:40,878
<i>Remember when Natalie said...</i>

358
00:19:40,979 --> 00:19:43,447
I have my Krav Maga class in half an hour.

359
00:19:43,849 --> 00:19:46,682
<i>Turns out Krav Maga is not a kind of yoga,</i>

360
00:19:46,785 --> 00:19:50,186
<i>It's a form of guerrilla street-fighting</i>
<i>developed by the Israeli army,</i>

361
00:19:55,093 --> 00:19:55,227
This is compliments
of those two gentlemen at the bar.

362
00:19:55,227 --> 00:19:58,492
This is compliments
of those two gentlemen at the bar.

363
00:19:59,064 --> 00:20:03,023
- "My knee!"
- "It's in my hair!"

364
00:20:05,404 --> 00:20:07,372
But isn't it nice to know
people are watching?

365
00:20:11,577 --> 00:20:15,536
- Oh, my God! Are you all right?
- What happened to you?

366
00:20:16,381 --> 00:20:17,609
Told the truth.

367
00:20:17,716 --> 00:20:20,378
Turns out the truth has
a mean roundhouse kick.

368
00:20:21,019 --> 00:20:22,179
Oh, man.

369
00:20:22,287 --> 00:20:24,983
Oh, well, you did the right thing.
I'm proud of you.

370
00:20:25,090 --> 00:20:26,614
I'm bleeding internally.

371
00:20:27,092 --> 00:20:29,117
Hey, Ted, you know what always
picks me up when I'm down?

372
00:20:29,228 --> 00:20:31,753
Other people's misfortune.
You missed something so amazing.

373
00:20:31,863 --> 00:20:34,889
Please, can we just have one person
in this whole bar who didn't see it?

374
00:20:35,000 --> 00:20:36,399
Fine.

375
00:20:36,935 --> 00:20:38,368
Are you okay?

376
00:20:38,770 --> 00:20:41,398
I really thought I was doing it
the good way this time.

377
00:20:41,573 --> 00:20:43,404
I guess there is no good way.

378
00:20:43,508 --> 00:20:46,136
Sometimes, no matter how hard
you try to do the right thing,

379
00:20:46,245 --> 00:20:50,477
you just end up flat on your back,
flailing around in a big pile of horse crap.

380
00:20:50,582 --> 00:20:53,881
- You saw it?
- My phone gets the Internet now.

381
00:20:55,921 --> 00:20:57,684
It's okay.

382
00:20:58,490 --> 00:21:00,549
<i>And that's how it ended with Natalie,</i>

383
00:21:00,659 --> 00:21:03,457
<i>No happily-ever-after,</i>
<i>Just a whole lot of hurt,</i>

384
00:21:03,562 --> 00:21:07,157
<i>And, just like that, all those</i>
<i>wonderful memories were replaced</i>

385
00:21:07,466 --> 00:21:08,763
<i>by this one,</i>

386
00:21:08,867 --> 00:21:12,860
<i>But, you know, bad as that night was,</i>
<i>within a year Natalie was married,</i>

387
00:21:13,038 --> 00:21:15,370
<i>And now she has three beautiful children,</i>

388
00:21:15,574 --> 00:21:19,305
<i>So that's the upside of hurt,</i>
<i>Sometimes it happens for a reason,</i>

389
00:21:20,445 --> 00:21:21,537
Wow.

390
00:21:22,648 --> 00:21:24,775
So you got beat up by a girl?

391
00:21:24,983 --> 00:21:27,281
Is that all you're taking away
from this story?

392
